From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:50:34 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 257/297] Meridian: Try with Claude on Windows

Windows builds again: StrongDevSignals() makes its macOS paths with
FilePath::FromASCII, and the linked-file test of Connect runs where
symbolic links can be made (POSIX).

Off macOS, OpenInClaude now does what the Mac does with Claude's link:
claude://claude.ai/new?q=<request> (or claude:// to just start it), the
same --meridian-test-claude-log for tests. On Windows the request is also
put on the clipboard, and the link is opened when claude:// is registered;
otherwise "Claude isn't on this computer yet." Linux keeps the plain stub.

"Get Claude for Mac" names the app for this system (Claude for Windows
there), and the showcase writes Ask's shortcut the system's way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
